# Pairs with CausalOrder. The bounded applied-identity record evicts the merged write along with its
# identity, so a dependent already applied no longer has its dependency.
MODULE: CausalOrderEvictionForgetsTheWrite
TARGET: CausalOrder
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: evicting an identity from the applied-identity record also forgets the merged write
PERTURBS: Forget
BOUNDS: Parts = {1}

--- FIND
    /\ h \in ids /\ ids' = ids \ {h}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rApplied, dlq, lost, dls, bApplied, bBuf, bDead, srcv, wake, booted>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ h \in ids /\ ids' = ids \ {h}
    \* MUTATION: the write goes too.
    /\ rApplied' = rApplied \ {h}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<dlq, lost, dls, bApplied, bBuf, bDead, srcv, wake, booted>>
--- END
